<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Makimuku</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Makimuku is an archaeological site in Sakurai, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> Prefecture, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, at the foot of Mount Miwa. In the early 3rd century it grew into a large planned settlement with a major building complex and some of the earliest keyhole-shaped tombs, including Hashihaka. Many scholars see it as the centre of Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himiko">Himiko</a>'s Yamatai or as the cradle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamato-court">Yamato kingship</a>.</p></div>
